WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.920
There are so many new beauty releases

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.990
happening all the time,

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:04.612
so we gathered some of the most-hyped

00:00:04.612 --> 00:00:06.990
products from May to test for ourselves.

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.220
Donni Davy, the head makeup
artist of "Euphoria,"

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.420
just came out with her own
makeup line, Half Magic,

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.070
and I bought a bunch of
products to test out.

00:00:14.070 --> 00:00:16.500
First up, we have these
Chromaddiction matte eye paints.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:17.690
They have a lot of pigment

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.750
and were really easy to layer and blend.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.000
They don't dry down too fast,

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.258
and you can use them as eyeliner,

00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:23.424
which is what I did.

00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:25.790
They have this reusable
wing guide, which was OK.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:27.770
I feel like it was a little too flimsy,

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:30.290
so I didn't get that
great of a wing with this.

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.490
This Glitterpill was so pretty,

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.870
and the applicator made it so easy to use.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:36.620
Plus, you don't have
to use a glitter base.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.770
It just dries down and stays put.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:40.090
The Light Trap glow powders

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.990
definitely do give you a nice glow,

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.890
and you can use them anywhere on the face.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:45.614
Like, I put this purple one on my eyes,

00:00:45.614 --> 00:00:47.797
and it looked so cool.

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:49.722
Of course, I also had
to get these iridescent

00:00:49.722 --> 00:00:51.380
face gems, which are self-adhering,

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.400
so you don't need any
glue for the first use.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.885
You will need glue if you reuse them.

00:00:55.885 --> 00:00:59.488
These are so easy to apply
and add such a cute sparkle.

00:00:59.488 --> 00:01:02.270
The last product I got was
the Magic Brownie Liptrik Kit.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.470
It has a darker and lighter lip liner,

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:06.410
so you can customize the lipstick.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:08.960
The lip liner is very smooth and creamy,

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.840
and this lipstick is super
comfortable on the lips.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:13.790
This brand as a whole really inspires you

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.580
to play with your makeup, which I love,

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.830
and I really liked the
products that I tried.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.110
I'm excited to see what
they come out with next.

00:01:20.110 --> 00:01:21.890
Danessa Myricks Beauty just released

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.070
this Skin Blurring Balm Powder.

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:26.400
I got the universal shade,
which is translucent,

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.321
and I also got the shade 4.

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:30.300
So, you can use this as a primer,

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.840
concealer and contour, a foundation,

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:35.566
or it can be used to set your foundation.

00:01:35.566 --> 00:01:38.060
I first tried the
universal one as a primer

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.770
under my go-to foundation.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:42.181
The texture is kind of strange.

00:01:42.181 --> 00:01:45.010
It blends in easily like a balm would,

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:49.212
but it dries down to, like,
a soft-matte powder finish.

00:01:49.212 --> 00:01:51.350
It really does blur a
lot of imperfections.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:53.760
My foundation went over this so smoothly,

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:55.580
and it did make it slightly more matte

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.890
than it usually looks, but I didn't mind.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:00.520
Then I tried the tinted
shade just as a foundation.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:02.500
It did take me a while to blend out,

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.075
but once I did, I really liked the finish.

00:02:05.075 --> 00:02:07.860
This is actually more full
coverage than I was expecting.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.901
I feel like it covered a lot!

00:02:09.901 --> 00:02:12.010
I did end up wearing
this for the entire day,

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:14.340
and I noticed that I was much less oily

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.410
at the end of the day than usual.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:18.090
It does have a bit of a learning curve,

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.732
but once you figure out
how to make this work

00:02:19.732 --> 00:02:22.290
for your skin, it's a really cool product.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.230
I don't know why it's taken me this long

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:26.590
to try the About-Face
Matte Fluid Eye Paints,

00:02:26.590 --> 00:02:28.120
but I'm finally doing it.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.610
These are liquid eye colors that come in

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:33.367
full-coverage mattes or sheer shades.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:35.160
Don't be scared by that orange swatch.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.540
That one is a sheer shade.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.680
The pigment in these is incredible.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.480
They're super easy to
apply and to blend out.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:43.080
You can build up the color if you want,

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:44.910
and it still feels lightweight.

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:46.720
Plus, I'm in love with this packaging.

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.070
These are amazing, and I need more colors.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:51.550
The Espressoh Glassy blush is one of those

00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.280
pH-reactive products.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.620
It goes from clear to a
pink tint on the skin.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:58.620
I first tried it over my foundation,

00:02:58.620 --> 00:02:59.862
and it started to break down

00:02:59.862 --> 00:03:01.730
the product I already had on.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:04.421
It was pilling so much.

00:03:04.421 --> 00:03:06.210
So we were off to a bad start.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:08.068
I tried it out on my bare skin,

00:03:08.068 --> 00:03:09.570
and it worked a lot better.

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:11.678
It's cute and a fun idea,

00:03:11.678 --> 00:03:13.036
but I'm not blown away by this.

00:03:13.036 --> 00:03:14.392
I would rather just get a blush

00:03:14.392 --> 00:03:16.910
that works on skin and over makeup.

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:19.760
This is the Bdellium large
rounded double dome blender,

00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.780
and it looks like a little mouth.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.312
It's basically like two brushes in one.

00:03:24.312 --> 00:03:26.500
It's supposed to blend
in product really fast

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:28.400
and give you an airbrushed finish.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:29.950
You can use it with any liquid,

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.430
cream, or powder product,

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:33.480
so I decided I would do a full face

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.738
with just this brush.

00:03:34.738 --> 00:03:37.452
I was immediately blown
away by how quickly

00:03:37.452 --> 00:03:39.580
and seamlessly this
blended in the product.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:43.033
Plus, this was, like, the
softest brush I've ever felt.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.120
You're supposed to do these
back-and-forth motions,

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.810
and I thought it would look so streaky,

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:49.981
but it just looked really
smooth and well blended.

00:03:49.981 --> 00:03:52.590
Because of the size, it is
a little difficult to use

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.770
for the more precise
products, like concealer,

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:57.080
but they do sell smaller
sizes of this brush.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:58.484
I loved it.

00:03:58.484 --> 00:04:00.440
This is the Saie Hydrabeam brightening

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.210
and hydrating under-eye concealer.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:05.010
It has a radiant finish,
which had me a little worried.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:06.440
I don't really think "radiant"

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.020
when I'm picking out a concealer.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:11.340
The coverage is light, a
little too light for my taste.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.960
I'm a medium- to full-coverage girl

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:14.060
when it comes to concealer,

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.677
but the finish is pretty and skin-like.

00:04:16.677 --> 00:04:19.321
It also looked good when
I set it with powder,

00:04:19.321 --> 00:04:22.270
but I absolutely hate
the applicator on this.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:24.400
In my opinion, it's too short.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.811
It is so stiff, and it
doesn't do a great job

00:04:26.811 --> 00:04:29.360
of picking up and spreading
the product around.

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:33.116
Other than that, this is a
very nice everyday concealer.

00:04:33.116 --> 00:04:35.510
These are the Tarte
Maracuja Juicy Lip Plumps,

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:38.602
and they're supposed to give
you a tingle-free plumping.

00:04:38.602 --> 00:04:40.670
They actually are so juicy.

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:42.220
Look at how shiny that is.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.950
My first reaction to these was that

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.790
they are incredibly fragile.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:47.185
Like, you want to be careful with how much

00:04:47.185 --> 00:04:49.340
pressure you're using,
because it will break.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:50.688
So I didn't love that.

00:04:50.688 --> 00:04:53.127
But these feel so good on the lips.

00:04:53.127 --> 00:04:55.262
Like, I could not stop
rubbing them together.

00:04:55.262 --> 00:04:57.669
It's so comfortable and hydrating.

00:04:57.669 --> 00:05:00.493
The plumping was actually
tingle-free for me.

00:05:00.493 --> 00:05:03.991
It just felt minty, like I
rubbed toothpaste on my lips.

00:05:03.991 --> 00:05:05.280
The plumping effect is subtle,

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.953
but I still really liked these.

